                                "sense_id": "b7d091d6-b96e-30c7-abb8-8ce68c20b7f8",
                                "text": "“And for everyone rooting for this little enemies-to-lovers tale...”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d5857b76-6fcd-46e0-b5b5-d86af9ef2c29",
                                "sense_id": "b7d091d6-b96e-30c7-abb8-8ce68c20b7f8",
                                "text": "I know that she never falls asleep before 2 a.m. and her favourite fanfic trope is enemies-to-lovers and she’s secretly a fan of Ariana Grande."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "dcdec52b-f285-4b1b-b103-df52f2a83fd7",
                                "sense_id": "b7d091d6-b96e-30c7-abb8-8ce68c20b7f8",
                                "text": "And that’s because Go Hex Yourself is a romantic masterpiece, and the sexiest, most bewitching take on enemies-to-lovers I’ve read in ages."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d2d10841-ad6f-453b-bf09-f344ad989da2",
                                "sense_id": "b7d091d6-b96e-30c7-abb8-8ce68c20b7f8",
                                "text": "When I read a book now, I think I'm much more trope-aware, because before I read fanfiction, I don't even think I fully understood what tropes were. So now I see, like, when a book has enemies-to-lovers, I see it, and I'm like, oh-oh."
                            }
                        ]
